But Steve isn't saying 1080p is bad. He's saying that nvidia was pushing 1440p and 4k as the next big thing. 3-4 generations later, you'd expect their low-tier cards to perform well at higher resolutions, but instead they chose to (in GN's opinion) cheap out on VRAM and bus width.

